Keep host ASLR pointers out of the Arm UML startup console

Docker's default seccomp profile refuses UML's attempt to disable host ASLR.
Each boot therefore places the host stack and stub at different addresses.
Those private pointers were printed in the captured guest console even though
the guest TASK_SIZE and execution were unchanged. Keep the guest limit
diagnostic and omit the host addresses.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a kernel diff under
consonance/harmony-linux/linux/patches/ per the repository's kernel-patch
exception.

---
--- a/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
@@ -425,12 +425,10 @@
 	 * from where the *host* put this process's stack. When that derivation
 	 * goes wrong the failure is silent and total: every guest mmap returns
 	 * -ENOMEM, so the first exec fails with -12 and nothing anywhere says
-	 * why. Print the three numbers -- one line, once, at boot -- because
-	 * reconstructing them afterwards requires a debugger on a host that may
-	 * be a phone.
+	 * why. Print the guest limit once at boot. Host stack and stub addresses
+	 * vary under ASLR and cannot enter the captured guest console.
 	 */
-	os_info("Address space: host top 0x%lx, stub at 0x%lx, guest TASK_SIZE 0x%lx\n",
-		stub_start + STUB_SIZE, stub_start, task_size);
+	os_info("Address space: guest TASK_SIZE 0x%lx\n", task_size);
 
 	/*
 	 * Before os_early_checks(), which is where a host that can only offer
